{"id": "EUVD-2026-80540", "enisaUuid": "cb202964-dcea-3cff-8884-4bb217ce8a57", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: buffer: Tie IIO dma fence lock lifetime to the fence\n\nThe `iio_dma_fence` implementation currently uses a lock embedded in the\n`iio_dmabuf_priv`. But the `iio_dma_fence` can outlive the\n`iio_dmabuf_priv`, which can cause a use-after-free.\n\nTie the lifetime of the lock to the lifetime of the fence by embedding them\nin the same struct.\n\nWe can't just hold a reference to the `iio_dmabuf_priv` from the\n`iio_dma_fence` since `iio_buffer_dmabuf_release()` might sleep and the\nfence release callback is not allowed to sleep.\n\nNote that the `dma_fence` framework now has an internal lock that gets used\nwhen the passing `NULL` for `lock` in `dma_fence_init()`, but in order to\nallow this patch to be backportable use an external lock.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:32:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:55:14", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6865d79fca17a80fbd60c12550ca9a5e0e20e0eb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/510497e31be4f241103507315a859e2085ccb081", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8b3e221590181a8beb3735bbabf166df02c839b5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f25ec4627d935dedfb5fe83bd2c2678cdcc19611"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rvmw-48g6-x73g", "CVE-2026-89940"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3b6717b8-abd2-3559-8d35-2d1827239872", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "885e1a03-8663-3e88-9661-72507afd6fd8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "a167139a-ccb5-3f98-a361-f6d2fc428296", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "a3783c09-56ef-3a99-93c2-3d2ad2a4fc37", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3e26d9f08fbe0b73e951a5e810fdb7a332b7e37f <6865d79fca17a80fbd60c12550ca9a5e0e20e0eb"}, {"id": "d8b936c8-d601-3ce6-91c7-5b7e1799e860", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "d9ca4ed5-97ff-377a-8c8c-7b694e662f8c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3e26d9f08fbe0b73e951a5e810fdb7a332b7e37f <8b3e221590181a8beb3735bbabf166df02c839b5"}, {"id": "e06a8cbe-1e2a-3a75-a026-97f577c3aa59", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "eaa18714-e89b-3eee-8d97-482254565823", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3e26d9f08fbe0b73e951a5e810fdb7a332b7e37f <f25ec4627d935dedfb5fe83bd2c2678cdcc19611"}, {"id": "edc2c57c-8d85-32b8-b8a2-379e1e9f0558", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3e26d9f08fbe0b73e951a5e810fdb7a332b7e37f <510497e31be4f241103507315a859e2085ccb081"}, {"id": "eec90185-97bc-33bc-b226-2d6c9e858e53", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1d0cdab2-2cb0-3969-a79e-5f3652d633a2", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}